What they did well:

The project demonstrates a solid understanding of secure coding principles and modern web application security practices.

The use of GitHub Copilot was effective and clearly documented, showing how AI can assist in both code generation and debugging.

Implementation of key security features like input validation, parameterized queries, JWT-based authentication, and RBAC was done correctly and thoughtfully.

The summary clearly explains vulnerabilities, solutions, and the AI’s role, which adds transparency and educational value.

Areas for improvement:

It would be helpful to include test coverage reports or logs to demonstrate that all security features were adequately tested.

Adding comments or inline documentation in critical sections (like authentication and input sanitization logic) could make the code easier to review and maintain.

The UI (if present) could have been briefly described or screenshotted to give context to the end-user flow and how security measures impact it.
